2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}+8{b}_{3} \\\\  & =8{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(4{b}_{3})+2{b}_{1}+2\\cdot 2(\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+4{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112656/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df96d21a-e1bc-5a9b-b528-d6e7b30d8451"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112855/selection/3b844ea1209a6e13bd3804dc62253be04259ef87dd1066f18c0375bde9c238b4" :answer/id #uuid "0ed0e007-c62d-599d-b28b-0e3805f57417" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112855/selection/d23de62cf2faf3c411a8bd33ee126444040bbc2b3534b8baf6c8761087506878" :answer/id #uuid "4fbab916-cd05-5434-87bf-004ec4f4c5fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112855/selection/28b6690659f1a51f8f3c7978a128974ecc78debfc3be034c322581f97d6c36de" :answer/id #uuid "2273a3b7-7955-5e9c-8a76-20b0a45cb8d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112855/selection/5968ac6e346a537742e3e969bc93b53c9ef3841f6e3931081497a8021d5ea5f9" :answer/id #uuid "4ea92aeb-d5ba-5ba6-8924-14d4d64b5b91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112855/selection/e90068a4c392e2adaa4bd596692a19aac8c021a136f9eac0f451317494dccf7d" :answer/id #uuid "fd42eacb-2b42-5268-816e-d659f2835cb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112855/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "42e2561b-4fdf-54ae-a64b-692264302692" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112855/selection/d23de62cf2faf3c411a8bd33ee126444040bbc2b3534b8baf6c8761087506878" :answer-field/choices ["q-112855/selection/3b844ea1209a6e13bd3804dc62253be04259ef87dd1066f18c0375bde9c238b4" "q-112855/selection/d23de62cf2faf3c411a8bd33ee126444040bbc2b3534b8baf6c8761087506878" "q-112855/selection/28b6690659f1a51f8f3c7978a128974ecc78debfc3be034c322581f97d6c36de" "q-112855/selection/5968ac6e346a537742e3e969bc93b53c9ef3841f6e3931081497a8021d5ea5f9" "q-112855/selection/e90068a4c392e2adaa4bd596692a19aac8c021a136f9eac0f451317494dccf7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112855" :question/id #uuid "ef9641c5-8258-5345-9a36-98913b3bf3a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-112855" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Multiplying the second equation by $-2$ and adding the equations, we get  \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}=-{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2(-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2})-3(-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2} \\\\  & =7{c}_{1}-12{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-112855/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e568b6fc-88f0-592b-a24d-e3286cfa5043"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112855"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
